        "comments": "Curator note: The reported karyotype for this species is 2n=60 (https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01934008). All chromosome pairs were identified during curation (4 macrochromosome pairs, 11 mid-sized chromosome pairs, and 15 microchromosome pairs). Because some of the larger chromosomes were above the size limit for INSDC submissions, they were split to be less than 2.1 Gbp, with splits made at the nearest gap, and the main chromosome numbers maintained, with the number after the underscore indicating the part split number. Haplotype 2, chromosome 15 has a possible misassembly around 723.7-771.4Mbp. With future investigation, one possibility is that it is really part of chromosome 2. Chromosome 11 in both haplotypes was very fragmented, especially in haplotype 2. In chromosome 1, haplotype 1, there are a number of large structural variant inversions and other rearrangements within the following coordinates: 1.13-1.47 Gbp in part 3; 574.8-613.5 Mbp and 1.25-1.26 Gbp in part 4, 472.0-530.0 Mbp in part 5",
